      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, determine the total depreciable amount by subtracting the salvage value from the cost of the machine: $145,000 - $15,000 equals $130,000. Next, divide this amount by the estimated useful life of 8 years, so $130,000 divided by 8 equals $16,250 in annual depreciation expense. For the year-end statements, you would record a depreciation expense of $16,250 for the CNC milling machine. Remember to also include a contra asset account that increases with accumulated depreciation for the sake of the audit trail.",
